From 6ca48f2cd27e8392be8d63cfdf88ba51a9a56957 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:45:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(spec_decode): use cumulative survival in copy_apply and
 cap single-req copy tile spill

Base: 1107 vLLM patch head 320021e3c4dbb202d911ab70e2cd924c75420488 (tree ed1bdb7a7684da33d403a055521ac0c4dd7ca670).

Rationale:
1. copy_apply_kernel previously gated CopyDrafter replacement against the sum of raw conditional DSpark probabilities (sum_{j=0}^{block-1} dspark_confidences[r, j]) rather than cumulative survival yield (sum_{j=0}^{block-1} prod_{i=0}^j dspark_confidences[r, i]). Because a 5-draft DSpark block with conditional confidences [0.70, 0.65, 0.60, 0.55, 0.50] has raw sum 3.00 but cumulative survival 1.6532, short 2- and 3-token copy continuations (expected yield 1.90 and 2.85 at 0.95 confidence) were rejected in favor of lower-yield DSpark proposals. Accumulating dspark_survival *= dspark_confidences[r, j] aligns copy_apply with AdaptiveVerificationManager.get_num_tokens.
2. AdaptiveVerificationManager._step_cost applied the high-concurrency coalescing discount (HIGH_ROW_COST_SCALE = 0.55 above HIGH_ROW_COST_KNEE = 16 rows) even when num_sampling_requests == 1. At row_cost = 0.035, a single-request 16-draft copy proposal at the 0.95 initial prior crossed 16 verification rows into 17 rows (24-row CUDA graph, 2 Tensor Core MMA waves of 16 rows). Applying SINGLE_REQ_TILE_SPILL_SCALE = 2.0 above 16 rows when num_sampling_requests <= 1 (and setting scheduled_drafts[0] = draft_budget directly in reallocate_drafts when num_reqs == 1) caps initial 0.95-prior single-request copy proposals at 15 drafts (16 rows = 1 MMA tile in the 16-row CUDA graph), while admitting all 16 drafts once online copy accuracy reaches >= 0.97 or when multiple requests share the batch (c2+).

Quality:
Bit-identical target and drafter arithmetic; temperature-0 greedy verification remains invariant to draft source and to the draft budget.

Tests:
- pytest tests/v1/spec_decode/test_copy_drafts.py tests/v1/core/test_copy_drafts_scheduler.py tests/v1/spec_decode/test_adaptive_verification.py tests/v1/worker/test_prepare_kernels.py (108 passed, 1 skipped across 2 boots on GB10; round 1 on the candidate-53 stack: 114 passed, 1 skipped in each of 2 container runs on GB10).

Round 1:
- Dropped rationale 3, the zero-confidence dead-row floor: _ZERO_CONFIDENCE_LOG_TAU, the has_copy_tail branch of dead_row_args, GPUModelRunner.declare_step_kernels declaring dead rows whenever a copy drafter exists, and their tests (the dead_row_args block of the tile-cap test, now test_single_request_tile_spill_caps_16th_copy_draft_at_16_rows, and the copy-drafter case of test_dead_row_caps_are_declared_before_the_manager_exists). The recipe sets SPARK_DS41F_DSPARK_DEAD_ROWS_TAU=0.2 on every shape, so dead_rows_enabled() is true and effective_dead_rows_tau() is positive (0.2, or 0.0633 once calibrated at row cost 0.035). There the floor's branch is never taken: dead_row_args already returns DeadRows(log tau) and marks a shrunk copy's -1 tail (confidence 0) as padding, and declare_step_kernels already declares dead rows. The floor acted only at tau 0, which no shape serves.
- Kept rationale 1 and 2 and their tests unchanged. The patch no longer touches vllm/v1/worker/gpu/model_runner.py or tests/v1/worker/test_prepare_kernels.py.
- Applies in candidate-53's series (0781, this patch, 0783, 0784, 0785) with git am; git diff --check clean.
- Measured on GB10 (sp8), spark-ds41f:candidate-50 with the candidate-53 files mounted, tau 0.2, same-session ABBA of two fresh containers an arm, the PR's 58-layer step workload: the c1 initial copy step at the 0.95 prior moves from the 24-row graph (17 rows) to the 16-row graph (16 rows), 150.3 -> 142.0 ms at TP3 (-5.5%, 95% interval -9.0..-7.6 ms; -5.8% with a 128 MiB cache wash) and 113.1 -> 107.7 ms at TP4 (-4.7%; -6.6% washed). The post-reject shrunk step is unchanged against the base at TP3 (-0.1% warm, +0.2% washed, inside the boot-to-boot spread). copy_apply admits 2- and 3-token copies against DSpark [0.70, 0.65, 0.60, 0.55, 0.50] (the base does not). No cell is slower. Against the original patch at tau 0.2 every policy output is identical: the step shapes, and in all 24 dead-row cases at tau 0.2 and its calibrated value (5- and 16-wide steps, three draft rows, drafts admitted or not) the DeadRows, cut, padding mask, input ids, logits indices and verified count. Of 36 cases, they differ only in the three 16-wide admitted cases at tau 0.

Upstream status: local speculative-decoding optimization for CopyDrafter and AdaptiveVerificationManager.
